      "lineNbr": 69,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-15T20:51:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Soong APIs used for exposing jar files from java_import to its consumers (e.g. java_library) do not allow for error reporting (other than panic) if the requested file is not available. All that they can do is return nil which is usually ignored. So, the only error that it will get is a compilation error because of missing classes which is completely unhelpful.\n\nModifying that API to support providing meaningful errors is a reasonably large amount of work that would have delayed this by at least a week if not more.\n\nReturning an empty and invalid jar with a weird name gives a slightly more helpful message and doesn\u0027t require any modifications to java_import.",
      "parentUuid": "cd059f7b_5627ebf0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 69,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 69,
        "endChar": 96
      },
      "revId": "ddcd4b77c574413844a641ba299da94d63121401",
