        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-15T20:51:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The value returned from this function is ignored if it is nil. So, we need to differentiate between three cases:\n1. Ignore the file.\n2. An empty file to be copied.\n3. A real file to be copied.\n\nAn OptionalPath provides no advantage over returning nil. We would still need to differentiate between 2 and 3.\n\nWe could make the return value a pair of (Path, bool) but using /dev/null just seemed less disruptive. My main concern with using that was whether it would work well with ninja.\n\nAlternatively, I did consider creating an empty file that could be used for copying from but there did not seem a good place to do that.",
      "parentUuid": "8aa82cbc_d7022c95",
