        "uuid": "af0832be_566b485b",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2210,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-16T17:08:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem with this is that they\u0027re just aliases and readers have to know about their definitions, e.g. on line 2275 it\u0027s used as a boolean. Even if that\u0027s fixed there\u0027s no type checking for boolean contexts. For this approach I\u0027d prefer to see a typed enum rather than an obfuscated bool, but then I think it\u0027s a bit of overkill here.\n\n\u003e (no completion)\n\n(My editor isn\u0027t so fancy and only does plain text completion, which means it happily completes in comments too. :) But sure, it\u0027s a valid point.)\n\n\u003e doesn\u0027t provide any additional information.\n\nA comment clarifies the meaning on the call site, same as this, but it\u0027s more informative in the sense that it doesn\u0027t hide what the value (and its type) actually is.\n\nSo I think this isn\u0027t an ideal pattern, but it is after all mostly a style issue - I won\u0027t block the CL over it.",
      "parentUuid": "ff66d91b_0414d1af",
